---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import "../../styles/global.css";
---
<Layout
  title="Hanfu vs Cheongsam: What's the Difference"
  description="Hanfu vs cheongsam compared. Cheongsam is the western name for the qipao — a 20th-century fitted dress, completely different from ancient loose Hanfu."
  canonicalUrl="https://www.dresses-hanfu.com/comparisons/cheongsam/"
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: "Comparisons", url: "/comparisons" }, { name: "Hanfu vs Cheongsam", url: "/comparisons/cheongsam" }]}
  articleSchema={{
    datePublished: "2026-08-01",
    dateModified: "2026-08-08",
    author: { "@type": "Person", "name": "Hanfu Dress Guide Editorial Team" }
  }}
>
  <SiteHeader active="/comparisons" />
  <main>
    <article>
      <section class="section" style="padding-bottom: 2rem;">
        <div class="container-narrow">
          <p style="font-size:0.8125rem;color:var(--color-muted);margin-bottom:1rem;"><a href="/" style="color:var(--color-accent);">Home</a> &rsaquo; <a href="/comparisons/" style="color:var(--color-accent);">Comparisons</a> &rsaquo; Hanfu vs Cheongsam</p>
          <h1>Hanfu vs Cheongsam: Two Names, One Big Difference</h1>
          <p class="lead" style="font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--color-muted);margin-top:1.5rem;line-height:1.55;">
            "Cheongsam" is simply the Cantonese name for the qipao — same garment, two names, one of which traveled West through Hong Kong. So comparing Hanfu and cheongsam means comparing the loose ancient Hanfu with the fitted modern qipao.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section" style="padding-top:0;">
        <div class="container-narrow">
          <h2>Why Two Names for the Qipao</h2>
          <h3 style="margin-top:1.5rem;">Qipao: the Mandarin name</h3>
          <p class="text-muted">
            Qipao (旗袍) is the Mandarin term, literally "banner gown," a reference to the Manchu banner system from the Qing dynasty.
          </p>
          <h3 style="margin-top:1.5rem;">Cheongsam: the Cantonese name</h3>
          <p class="text-muted">
            Cheongsam is the Cantonese pronunciation, which spread to the West via Hong Kong and the overseas Chinese communities in the mid-20th century. Both names describe the identical short, fitted, buttoned dress popularized in 1920s-1950s Shanghai.
          </p>

          <h2 style="margin-top:3rem;">Hanfu vs Cheongsam (Qipao)</h2>
          <div style="overflow-x:auto;">
            <table class="size-ref-table" style="margin-top:1rem;">
              <thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Hanfu</th><th>Cheongsam (Qipao)</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td><strong>Age</strong></td><td>3,000+ years old</td><td>About a century old</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Silhouette</strong></td><td>Loose, layered, flowing</td><td>Fitted, sheath-like</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Collar</strong></td><td>Cross-over wrapping</td><td>Standing high collar, frog buttons</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Waist</strong></td><td>Sash-tied, adjustable</td><td>Tailored, fixed</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Cuts</strong></td><td>Rectangles, zero-waste</td><td>Western-influenced contour cutting</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <h2 style="margin-top:3rem;">Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-muted">
            If you see a form-fitting, buttoned, high-collar sheath dress, you're looking at a qipao/cheongsam — not Hanfu. If you see a loose, wrapped, crossed-collar robe with a sash, that's Hanfu. They represent two very different moments in Chinese dress history, and neither is a subset of the other.
          </p>

          <div style="margin-top:3rem;padding:2rem;background:var(--color-accent-light);border-radius:var(--radius-md);">
            <p style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;font-family:var(--font-display);">More Comparisons</p>
            <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:0.75rem;margin-top:1rem;">
              <a href="/comparisons/kimono/" class="btn btn-outline">Hanfu vs Kimono</a>
              <a href="/comparisons/qipao/" class="btn btn-outline">Hanfu vs Qipao</a>
              <a href="/comparisons/hanbok/" class="btn btn-outline">Hanfu vs Hanbok</a>
              <a href="/comparisons/" class="btn btn-outline">All Comparisons</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</Layout>